docs {
  # Eventing Tests
  
  End-to-end tests for the SIF event distribution flow, including
  the "Get Next and Pop" message delivery pattern (SIF §9.3.1).
  
  ## What This Tests
  
  1. Creates a complete domain/solution/zone infrastructure
  2. Creates a provider environment with PROVIDE ACL for TESTOBJECT1s
  3. Creates 3 consumer environments with queues
  4. Only consumers 1 and 3 get SUBSCRIBE ACL + subscriptions (consumer 2 does not)
  5. Provider emits an event for TESTOBJECT1s
  6. Verifies queue details — consumers 1 and 3 have messages, consumer 2 does not
  7. Consumer3 retrieves a message (Get Next) and ACKs it (Get Next and Pop)
  
  ## Prerequisites
  
  - All services running (gateway, environment-service, events-connector, queue-service, subscription-service)
  - Admin credentials configured in .env
  
  ## Run Order
  
  Tests are numbered and must be run in sequence:
  - 00-09: Infrastructure setup (domain, solution, zone, environments, ACLs, queues, subscriptions)
  - 10: Provider emits event
  - 11a-11c: Verify queue details for each consumer
  - 12a: Consumer3 retrieves next message (idempotent — repeated calls return same message)
  - 12b: Consumer3 ACKs the message and gets next (SIF "Get Next and Pop" §9.3.1)
}

